<P>Finally, I had a spare minute or two, and the main question seemed to =
be how=20
to introduce mod_python. I've decided to focus on a high level overview =
of=20
mod_python's features and benefits.</P>
<H3>What is Mod_python?</H3>
<P>Mod_python is actually several things:</P>
<UL>
  <LI>a loadable Apache module which embeds the Python interpreter=20
  (<CODE>libpython</CODE>), thereby providing the ability to execute =
Python code=20
  in-process by Apache.=20
  <LI>a handler of Apache's request processing phases, allowing for any =
phase of=20
  the request to be implemented in Python. It also allows filters and =
connection=20
  handlers to be implemented in Python.=20
  <LI>an interface to a subset of the Apache API, allowing the ability =
to call=20
  internal Apache functions from Python. This provides access to =
internal server=20
  information and ability to take advantage of Apache server facilities =
such as=20
  logging.=20
  <LI>a collection of tools for developing web applications. It provides =
a set=20
  of standard handlers: Publisher, PSP, and CGI each providing an =
alternative=20
  development framework, as well as a set of utility objects and =
functions for=20
  cookie processing, session management, and other things common in web=20
  development. </LI></UL><!--=0A=
