  that we shouldn't have to deal with perl or php especially when =
writing a=20
  large-scale web-applications. Don't get me wrong, the problem with =
perl is not=20
  because it's not powerful enough, but unlike Python, Perl just doesn't =
lend=20
  itself to uniform coding and easy-to-read-and-maintain-ability that is =
key to=20
  large-scale web-applications that tend to be written by numerous =
developers=20
  over a long time.<BR><BR>I wrote Zope programs (Python). Zope is =
excellent in=20
  terms of productivity and the Zope http server is nothing to sneeze =
at, but I=20
  have to admit that if my target clients are in the thousands or more, =
Apache=20
  is more scalable.<BR><BR>Good job! </DIV>
