SPAN><BR><BR>
  <DIV class=3Dcommenttext>I'm very excited to hear this news. I've =
always thought=20
  python to be a great language to develop in. But I've always been =
skeptical=20
  about Python and web development. I come from the Java world where =
there are=20
  some core standards that all app. servers adhere to. That makes =
learning,=20
  teaching, and deploying web applications in java so much =
easier.<BR><BR>In=20
  Python, there are no such standards, and there are a handful of =
promising, but=20
  totally different, development environments (mentioned above in your =
article,=20
  too).<BR><BR>For Python to really succeed in an area that I think it's =

  destined to, there must emerge some dominant standard web development=20
  framework. The new mod_python, with support for cookies and sessions, =
might=20
  just be this standard development environment.<BR><BR>So thanks for =
adding in=20
  cookies and sessions. I want to replace all my PHP and Perl scripts =
with=20
  Python scripts. And one day, all of my Java will be gone. I can't =
wait!=20
  </DIV></LI></UL><!-- thread_footer.view --></DIV><!-- end div.feedback =
